    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0293" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg269"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Harvey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 131.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 22, 1864</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatches—No. 260, of the 20th
                    ultimo, and No. 261, of the 22d ultimo—have been received. The latter has been
                    referred for perusal to the Secretary of the Navy.</p>
                <pb facs="0294" n="270" xml:id="pg270"/>
                <p>The promptness and energy manifested by the authorities at the Azores in carrying
                    out the instructions of the home government concerning rebel cruisers which may
                    seek to rendezvous at those islands is very satisfactory, and your own activity
                    and vigilance in connexion with these matters is highly appreciated.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James E. Harvey</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.<hi rendition="#italic">,
                            Lisbon.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
